## Pull requests and CHANGELOG

- **One commit per PR branch** before merge: do not stack many small commits (`fix lint`, `docs`, follow-ups). Fold changes into a single commit (`git reset --soft origin/main` + one commit, or amend the existing PR commit when hooks adjust files and the branch is not shared). See [CONTRIBUTING.md § One commit per pull request](../../CONTRIBUTING.md#one-commit-per-pull-request).
- **Do not** paste a full PR body every turn. If the turn might become a PR, **ask once** if the user wants paste-ready PR text.
- **After they confirm:** load **drafting-pulp-tool-pr** skill — PR text follows `.github/PULL_REQUEST_TEMPLATE.md` verbatim; include suggested commit (`Assisted-By:` + `Signed-off-by:` per `.github/commit-message-template.txt`) and **`CHANGELOG.md`** under `[Unreleased]` when notable — **same turn**.
- **No** `CHANGELOG` edits on every debug fix unless the user asks.
- **Merge gate:** **100% diff coverage** on the PR diff (`make test-diff-coverage`). If it fails, use **troubleshooting-pulp-tool-ci** (diff coverage section).

## After code changes (mandatory)

1. `make lint` → fix issues (or run `make format` first for Ruff import/format fixes)
2. `pre-commit run --all-files` → **loop** until **zero** failures (commit stage: lock-check, ruff, pylint, mypy, pip-audit, yamllint, shellcheck, codespell, hadolint)
3. `make test` (full suite) → **loop** until green
4. `git fetch origin` → `pre-commit run --hook-stage pre-push --all-files` (or `make test-diff-coverage`) → **loop** until diff-cover and Checkton pass

Shortcut before a PR: `make pre-commit-ci` (runs steps 2 and 4 after you have green tests).

Do not treat the branch as PR-ready without clean pre-commit (commit + pre-push stages), green tests, and passing diff-cover.

